                "text": "SGF first-week survey of establishments with at least 100 workers, in weekly hours, read at the survey week's midpoint (the 4th). The 0.2-hour reading error is fixed: the survey averages thousands of establishments, and a free error would trade off against hours volatility.\n\nStatistique g\u00e9n\u00e9rale de la France, Bulletin July-September 1938, p. 511, Table A: Average weekly hours in establishments occupying at least 100 persons, first-week survey of each month. [1]",
